      "seed": 43054296,
      "version": 639,
      "versionNonce": 240550872,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785906142320,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why static methods do not allow to access instance variable \n======================================================\n\n1. Because instance variable are accesses using calling object \nand compiler do not know which object's data static method is \naccessing as static methods are called using class Name .\n\n2. Even if programmer can call it using object (syntactically correct)\nat bit level jvm replace it with class name .\n\n3. However, a static method can access instance variables by\n using an object reference .\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why static methods do not allow to access instance variable \n======================================================\n\n1. Because instance variable are accesses using calling object \nand compiler do not know which object's data static method is \naccessing as static methods are called using class Name .\n\n2. Even if programmer can call it using object (syntactically correct)\nat bit level jvm replace it with class name .\n\n3. However, a static method can access instance variables by\n using an object reference .\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
