      "version": 725,
      "versionNonce": 153151400,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785907764243,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. static blocks has two special feature \n\n--> It will run automatically .\n--> run exactly one time .\n\n2. when we make the use of class first time, that is when \nclass loads in the memory . \n\n3. static blocks cannot access instace variable coz it run\nbefore object creation .\n\n4. Program can have multiple static blocks and will execute in the order \nthey are implemented .\n\n5. programmer cannot use return in static block as it is not a method .\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. static blocks has two special feature \n\n--> It will run automatically .\n--> run exactly one time .\n\n2. when we make the use of class first time, that is when \nclass loads in the memory . \n\n3. static blocks cannot access instace variable coz it run\nbefore object creation .\n\n4. Program can have multiple static blocks and will execute in the order \nthey are implemented .\n\n5. programmer cannot use return in static block as it is not a method .\n\n\n\n\n",
